Effective date: 15 October 2026
Version: 2026-10-15

This Hooxie License Agreement (the "Agreement") is a binding contract between Delexo ("Delexo," "we," "us," or "our") and the person or entity that downloads, installs, pays for, accesses, or uses Hooxie, the hooxie.com website, or related installers, updates, and services (the "Software"). "You" and "your" mean that person or, if you accept for an organization, that organization and the individual who accepts.

Hooxie is a Windows desktop product published by Delexo at https://hooxie.com. Support: support@delexo.store. The same text is posted at https://hooxie.com/license.

READ THIS AGREEMENT. IT LIMITS WARRANTIES, LIMITS OUR LIABILITY, REQUIRES YOU TO COVER CERTAIN CLAIMS AGAINST US, AND SENDS MOST DISPUTES TO INDIVIDUAL ARBITRATION UNLESS YOU OPT OUT IN TIME. IT ALSO SAYS THAT YOU, NOT DELEXO, ARE RESPONSIBLE FOR WHAT A CODING AGENT READS, CHANGES, AND RUNS, AND FOR ANY USE OF A WINDOW THAT IS LEFT OUT OF A SCREEN CAPTURE.

If you do not agree, do not download, install, buy, or use the Software. If you already installed it, stop using it and uninstall it.

A short reading aid appears first. The numbered sections are the contract. If the reading aid and a numbered section differ, the numbered section controls.


READING AID

- One paid license unlocks one computer. Copying the app or the license file does not unlock another computer.
- Hooxie does not replace a Cursor plan, a Cursor account, or any other agent service you connect.
- The Software is provided as is. We do not promise that an agent edit is correct, that the window will stay hidden, or that the Software will keep working after Windows or Cursor changes.
- Our liability for a claim about a computer's license is limited to the amount you paid for that license, except where the law does not allow that limit.
- You are responsible for prompts, files, screens, voice, and for rules set by schools, employers, exam administrators, and other services.
- Most disputes go to individual arbitration, not a class action, unless you opt out within 30 days or a mandatory consumer law says otherwise.


