2. WHO THIS BINDS

2.1 You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of legal majority where you live, whichever is higher. The Software and the Website are not directed to children under 13. You must not let a child under 13 use them or send us a child's personal information. If you are under 18, do not accept this Agreement.

2.2 If you use the Software for a company or other organization, you represent that you can bind it. "You" then includes that organization. If you lack authority, you must not accept. If you use the Software anyway, you accept personally.

2.3 You may not accept this Agreement, buy a license, or use the Software if you are barred under the export and sanctions section, or if a court or government order prohibits you from doing so.

2.4 This Agreement gives you a copyright license. It is not a sale of goods except to the extent a mandatory consumer law treats digital content as goods. Title to the Software does not pass to you.


3. DEFINITIONS

"Agent" means a coding assistant or model service you choose to receive a prompt, including a Cursor agent when you connect Cursor.

"Capture exclusion" means a Windows setting, including a display-affinity or exclude-from-capture flag, that asks Windows to leave the Hooxie window out of ordinary screen capture. In the product this is the state in which Detectable is off. Marketing text sometimes calls that state undetectable mode.

"Computer" means the single Windows device identified for licensing as described in section 6.

"Cursor" means the Cursor desktop application, account, and related services offered by Anysphere, Inc. or its affiliates. Cursor is a third-party product. Delexo does not own it and does not speak for it.

"Device identifier" means a one-way hash of the Windows MachineGuid, used to tie a license to one Computer. The hash is not your name.

"Input" means anything you or your Computer submit through the Software, including prompts, keystrokes, files, folder paths, clipboard contents, voice audio or transcribed speech, screenshots, screen descriptions, project files the Agent reads, and settings.

"Output" means text, code, diffs, tool actions, or other results returned by an Agent or produced from Input.

"License file" means the local record, including license.json, that stores the proof that this Computer is licensed.

"Paid license" means the one-time right, after a successful Stripe checkout or a promotional code that Delexo honors, to use the licensed features on one Computer.

"Stripe" means Stripe, Inc. and its affiliates, which process payment.

"Website" means hooxie.com and the pages Delexo serves for Hooxie, including terms, privacy, refunds, help, and this Agreement.


4. WHAT HOOXIE IS

4.1 Hooxie is a Windows overlay that keeps a prompt on the display and can send Input to an Agent you configure. It can attach files, refer to a project folder, use a microphone for voice, and include screen context when you turn that on. It runs on your Computer. A local page is served on the loopback address http://127.0.0.1:47321 for the overlay and related local functions.

4.2 Hooxie is an interface. It is not the Agent, not a model provider, and not a substitute for your own review of code. The Agent can read, edit, and run things in a folder you select. You choose that folder. You are responsible for what the Agent reads, edits, and runs there.

4.3 A paid license is a limited copyright license. It is not a sale of our intellectual property and not an assignment of any right except the limited rights in section 5. We reserve every right we do not expressly grant.

4.4 Features can differ by version, by Windows build, by what Cursor or another Agent allows, and by whether this Computer has a paid license. Descriptions on the Website, in a demo, in a video, or in a conversation explain the product in ordinary language. They are not a warranty, a service-level agreement, or a promise that a particular capture tool, proctoring product, remote-desktop product, or future operating-system change will behave in a particular way. A statement that a normal screen share does not see the window describes the intended Windows capture flag. It is not a promise that every tool, person, camera, or later Windows change will fail to see the window.

4.5 The price of a paid license is 5.99 United States dollars once for one Computer, unless a promotional code changes the amount Stripe charges. Taxes may be added. There is no subscription and no renewal of that charge. The paid license does not include a Cursor subscription, model usage, API usage, or any other third-party fee.

4.6 Node.js 22.13 or newer is required unless a given installer states otherwise. You are responsible for installing the system software the version you use requires.

4.7 If you have trouble using the Website with assistive technology, email support@delexo.store with the page address and the tool you use. We will use that report to try to remove the barrier. That process does not waive a non-waivable accessibility right, and it is not a representation that the Website conforms to a named technical standard.


