22. PRIVACY AND DATA-PROTECTION LAWS

22.1 The privacy policy at https://hooxie.com/privacy is part of this Agreement. If this section and that policy disagree about a privacy practice, the policy controls.

22.2 On your Computer, the widget handles prompts, attached files, voice, and screenshots, and can send them to the Agent you configured. The Website does not receive the text of your prompts. Project files are not uploaded to the Hooxie Website as part of ordinary use.

22.3 What we receive is limited: the billing email address, whether the one-time payment for this Computer is complete, the amount, a promotional code Stripe redeems, and messages you send to support. Card numbers go to Stripe, not to us.

22.4 We do not sell personal information. We do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. We do not place an advertising tracker on the Website for that purpose. We do not use prompts to train a model.

22.5 Where the EU General Data Protection Regulation or the UK GDPR applies, Delexo is controller only of the billing and support information we actually receive. We are not the controller of Input that stays on your Computer or that you send to an Agent. The legal bases for the information we hold are performance of this Agreement, legitimate interests in licensing, fraud prevention, and support, and compliance with legal duties such as tax and accounting. You may request access, correction, erasure, restriction, or portability, and you may object to processing based on legitimate interests, by emailing support@delexo.store. You may lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. You may withdraw consent where processing is based on consent, without affecting processing that already happened lawfully.

22.6 Stripe may process payment data in the United States and in other countries under Stripe's terms and its own transfer tools. Prompts are not part of a transfer to us, because we do not receive them.

22.7 Where the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act, applies, the categories we collect are identifiers (an email address), commercial information (amount, promotional code, and whether the Computer is licensed), and the contents of support messages you choose to send. Sources are you and Stripe. Purposes are providing the license, receipts, fraud prevention, refunds, and support. We do not sell or "share" personal information as those words are defined in that law. We do not use or disclose sensitive personal information for purposes that give you a right to limit use beyond what we already avoid. You may request to know, delete, or correct by emailing support@delexo.store. We will verify using the purchase email. We will not discriminate against you for exercising those rights. You may use an authorized agent if you provide the proof that law requires.

