26. THE LOCAL LISTENER

26.1 The overlay listens on the loopback interface at http://127.0.0.1:47321 unless a build documents a different local port. Loopback is intended to be reachable from processes on your own Computer, not from the public Internet.

26.2 You will not forward that port, tunnel it, bind it on a public interface, or weaken a firewall so that another machine can drive your Agent. If you do, you are responsible for every resulting action, including commands run in your folders, data sent to an Agent, and charges on your Cursor account.

