43.3 Severability. If a provision is held unenforceable, a court or arbitrator will modify it to the smallest extent that makes it enforceable, or will sever it if modification is not possible. The rest of the Agreement stays in effect. Section 37 contains its own rule for the class waiver.

43.4 No waiver. A failure or a delay in enforcing a provision is not a waiver. A waiver must be specific and in writing to bind the party giving it. A waiver on one occasion is not a waiver on the next.

43.5 Interpretation. Headings are for convenience only. The word "including" means "including without limitation." "Or" is inclusive unless the sentence says otherwise. This Agreement is in English. A translation, if we publish one, is for convenience, and the English text controls if they differ. No rule that construes a contract against the drafter applies. "Will" and "shall" both mean a duty. A reference to a statute includes that statute as amended and any successor statute. A reference to "days" means calendar days unless the sentence says business days.

43.6 Independent parties. You and Delexo are independent contractors. This Agreement does not create a partnership, a joint venture, a franchise, an employment relationship, or an agency. Neither party can bind the other. There are no third-party beneficiaries except the Covered Persons, who may enforce sections 29, 30, and 31.

43.7 Notices to you may be sent to the purchase email or posted on the Website, and they are effective when sent or posted. Notices to Delexo under this Agreement must be emailed to support@delexo.store and are effective when we receive them. If a statute requires a postal address for a particular kind of notice and this page does not print one, we will provide a current postal address for that statutory purpose on written request. A consumer in California may also write to the Complaint Assistance Unit of the Division of Consumer Services of the California Department of Consumer Affairs at 1625 North Market Blvd., Suite N 112, Sacramento, California 95834, or telephone (800) 952-5210 or (916) 445-1254.

43.8 Export of the dispute. You will bring a private claim only in the forum section 37 or section 38 allows.

43.9 Reservation of remedies. Our rights are cumulative except where this Agreement says a remedy is exclusive. We are not obliged to monitor prompts, Capture exclusion, or Agent actions. If we choose to investigate a reported abuse, that choice does not create a duty to investigate the next report.

43.10 Headings of mandatory notices. Where this Agreement restates a statutory guarantee, including in section 35.4, the restatement is there to meet a disclosure practice. It does not reduce the statute.


44. EVENTS OUTSIDE A PARTY'S CONTROL

Neither party is in breach for a delay or a failure caused by an event beyond its reasonable control, including a failure or a policy change of Cursor, Stripe, a model provider, Windows, a certificate authority, or a public network, and including a change in law, a labor disruption not limited to that party's own employees, a natural disaster, a utility failure, or an act of government. The affected party will make a reasonable effort to limit the effect and to resume. This section does not excuse your duty to pay for a license that was delivered, and it does not excuse your duty to keep backups or to decide what Input to send.


